# UX source of truth

When building or changing any screen, widget, icon, color, copy layout, or navigation, match `docs/UX` exactly. Read the matching mockup before writing UI. Do not invent a different layout, icon set, illustration, or visual style.

## Files

- Spec: `docs/UX/Pocket_Tutor_Detailed_UI_Specification.md`
- Screens: `A. Launch & Onboarding.png` through `I. Common States & Components.png`, plus `Exams.png`
- Splash: `Porar Sathi Study App Splash Screen.png`
- Launcher icons: `Icons-1.png` (master), `Icons-2.png` (Android sizes), `Icons-3.png.png` (iOS sizes)

Screen boards are numbered 1–137 and match the spec section titles.

## How to apply

- Layout, spacing, controls, empty states, and on-screen icons come from the PNG for that screen.
- Behavior, states, and copy the PNG does not show come from the UI spec.
- If a PNG and the written spec disagree on what is visible, follow the PNG.
- Use the supplied launcher mark: blue rounded square, open book, calendar, green check. Do not redraw it.
- Subject rows use the colored icons shown on the boards (Physics, Chemistry, Math, Biology, Bangla, English, and the rest).
- Bottom navigation on the main shell is Today, Plan, Syllabus, Progress, More, unless the specific board shows a different slot for that flow (some exam, revision, and backlog boards show Exams).
- Primary actions are full-width blue buttons. Status uses text plus color (On Track, Due, Overdue), never color alone.
- Support English and বাংলা. Keep Bangla labels natural and consistent with the spec glossary.
- Light, dark, and system themes must stay inside the same visual system.

Product name on the splash asset and launcher sheets is **Porar Sathi / পড়ার সাথী**. In-app screen boards are labeled **Pocket Tutor**. Match the asset you are implementing; do not introduce a third name or icon.
